      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bridgeton began as Lockwood Mills, later nicknamed Sodom because of the town’s notorious drinking and fighting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridgeton%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Farmers once paid milling services with a sixth of their grain, but a 1853 law cut it to an eighth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridgeton%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s iconic covered bridge burned in 2005, then was faithfully reconstructed and reopened in October 2006.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
